00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.980
Is it just me or am I starting to notice a pattern here?

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:50.920
*The Best Intro Ever*

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:57.840
MP: Hello Internet, welcome to Film Theory! The show that always sweats the small stuff. Speaking of sweat,

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:05.540
You know what I hate? Katsuki Bakugou. With the sandy-haired, hyper-aggressive bully from My Hero Academia. I know, I know, I get it!

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:10.900
He's learning to accept others and blah blah blah blah blah, but seriously dude, get over yourself!

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.240
Katsuki: "I don't need any of your protection, dammit!"

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:18.040
It's one thing to be stubborn and cocky but jeez, dial it back once in a while.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.040
Katsuki: "I just wanna say:

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.040
I'm gonna win."

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:22.680
Other Charaters: "Get off the stage!"

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:29.620
But even I have to admit that, despite his obnoxious personality, he has got himself one heck of a fascinating superpower

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.520
While quirks in the Hero Academia universe can range from

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:36.360
Godlike to totally useless, when Bakugo spun the wheel,

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.709
He definitely landed closer to the godly end of the scale. If you don't know the show,

00:01:40.709 --> 00:01:43.920
Let me tell ya, he's got himself the power to produce massive

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:50.820
Explosions, but the way that he activates that power, like Bakugou himself, is um less than pleasant.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:55.860
You see, Bakugo's quirk isn't just making things magically explode. He's no Yoshikage Kira.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.400
*To Be Continued Meme Soundtrack*

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.180
Instead, Bakugou's explosions are a byproduct of his actual quirk,

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:11.040
Which is that he sweats nitroglycerin, or to be more specific a substance, very similar to nitroglycerin, which he can detonate at will

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:15.360
Katsuki: "Since you're such a stalker, by now you know how my quirk, Explosion, works.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.940
I secrete nitroglycerin-like sweat from my hands and make it blow up."

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:23.820
MP: Essentially, the sweatier he gets, the bigger his explosions are. And over the course of the series,

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:27.240
We've seen Bakugo make some pretty darn big

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:34.240
Earth-shattering kabooms. Even without his special grenade gloves that store up his uh fluids to create bigger blasts.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.320
So of course, all this raises the obvious question:

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:42.480
How much would Bakugou have to sweat to create blasts as big and powerful as he does?

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.760
Welp, you outta know by now that that's the exact sort of insane

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:51.089
Question that I answer on this channel. So roll on some Old Spice and make sure that you're wearing an undershirt,

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:57.389
*Some movie quote I can't quite hear that's about sweat* since today, we're literally working up a sweat to prove how hot under the collar this anime

00:02:57.489 --> 00:03:05.099
Character gets. And spoiler alert! He's producing more sweat daily than the gaming room at your local anime convention

00:03:05.099 --> 00:03:07.798
Oh, yeah, it's that bad. To begin,

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:15.060
We're told that Bakugou's sweat is basically identical to nitroglycerin. And since science knows a lot about how much nitroglycerine

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:20.120
Expands when it explodes, I'm measuring a given explosion from the anime. We can work out pretty easily

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:24.090
Exactly how sweaty Bakugou would have to get to produce it.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:28.439
Now, one thing I'm not gonna do is look at what Bakugou can do in his hero costume

00:03:28.599 --> 00:03:33.569
since those grenade gauntlets of his are designed to store his sweat over time, thus making their

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:38.800
explosive power more based on how long he's been wearing them as opposed to how much he's actually sweating.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.140
That said, the newest season of the anime has given us a great benchmark.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:48.840
In season 3 episode 3, we're given a quirk training montage where each character is trying to push their quirks to the limit in order to

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:52.880
Expand their powers. We're expressly told that Bakugo is

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:04.680
So, not only are these visually the largest fireballs that he produces in the series,

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:09.300
We also know that Bakugo is intentionally pushing himself to his limits here to unleash his full strength;

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:14.380
both in terms of explosion size as well as how fast he's making those explosions happen.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.920
At first, I thought I could just measure the blasts using Bakugou himself

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:23.310
as the measuring stick, since he's right there and we know that his canon height is exactly a hundred and seventy two centimeters,

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:26.600
Based on the character stat cards that pop up between commercial breaks.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:31.640
However, I wanted to be as precise as possible which, when it comes to Bakugou, is a bit of an issue.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:35.820
He has that super saiyan perm thing going on that makes it hard to figure out how exactly

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:39.920
his height's being measured. And he almost never stands up straight

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:44.099
Lucky for us though, Bakugou is not the only measuring stick that we have at our disposal here.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:49.480
He's standing next to an oil drum—the exact same kind of oil drum that his fellow

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:54.659
Classmate, Todoroki, is using for his training. And with his good posture and flat haircut,

00:04:54.659 --> 00:04:58.709
This icy hot honor student makes for a much better measuring stick.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.440
We know that from heel to head, Todoroki stands at

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:06.940
176 centimeters tall. That means, using his height in this manga profile picture as a baseline,

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:12.420
We can determine his pupillary distance or the distance between the centers of the pupils of his eyes.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:15.960
A measurement that's often taken by optometrists during eye appointments.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:22.040
On average, male pupillary distances are between five point three centimeters and seven point seven centimeters

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:24.500
And Todoroki's pupils are exactly

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:27.020
7.62 centimeters apart

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:32.190
So it falls right in that range. This measurement can then be translated over to the training montage

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:39.660
To measure the barrel from side to side in this shot. Which gives us a barrel diameter of seventy nine point eight eight centimeters.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:46.180
Finally, we can apply those barrel measurements to the one standing next to Bakugou to measure the diameter of the fireball.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:47.340
Aaaaaannnnddd

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.480
Here's where we run into one other snag.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:54.570
You see, we're never actually shown the full scale of the fireball that Bakugou creates.

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:58.320
Despite it being a distant shot that we can clearly tell goes above the treeline.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:04.319
So we're just gonna have to settle for measuring the part of the fireball that we can actually see in this flat on shot but

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.870
Trust me even that it is more than enough

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:12.100
If we cut a chunk off the fireball starting at the widest point before it goes past the edge of the screen,

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:17.940
we get a dome that's 2,545 centimeters across by 716 centimeters tall.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:24.600
Plugging those numbers into this formula, which measures the volumes of spherical caps, gives us a total volume of two

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:32.560
thousand four hundred twenty-eight point two cubic meters or two million four hundred and twenty eight thousand two hundred and seven liters of

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:36.900
Exploding gas. That certainly sounds like a lot, but to truly understand what that means,

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:39.660
Let's dig a little deeper. Doing a little research,

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:46.830
We know that when it explodes, nitroglycerin expands to a little over twelve hundred times the volume of its original liquid form.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:49.440
So all we have to do is divide the volume of the

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:56.369
Explosion by twelve hundred to see just how much sweat Bakugou would need to produce it. Leaving us with a final grand total of

00:06:56.370 --> 00:07:03.569
A whopping two thousand twenty three and a half liters of sweat.To put that in perspective, an average human

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:10.000
Produces between point eight and one point four liters of sweat during an hour of exercise.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:17.060
Or, for a fair point of comparison since Bakugou's using hot water to open up his sweat glands, an average person produces

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:22.980
Just one liter of sweat after fifteen minutes in a steam room. Bakugou is sweating at least

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:27.420
2,000 times that amount in the five seconds between

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:33.700
Explosions in this scene—and remember, that's just part of the fireball. The whole thing is three to four times the size of what we

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:37.600
Can actually measure which means that Bakugou is probably producing closer to six

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:42.460
Thousand liters of sweat in five seconds, from just the palms of his hands.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:48.580
That's about a hundred and fifty times the total volume of liquid contained in the average human body.

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:55.580
And if a real person were truly sweating that much liquid, they'd shrivel up and die like a prune in a fraction of a second.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:59.300
But let's just ignore that problem for a moment and assume that Bakugou's quirk somehow

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:04.999
Compensates for this rapid fluid loss by other means; the same way it prevents his explosions from blowing his hands off.

00:08:04.999 --> 00:08:08.629
I mean after all, this is a universe where a guy's whole body can be made out of

00:08:08.819 --> 00:08:15.438
Teleporting mist or a guy's face can be made out of flame or a guy could have teeth that turn into magically long blades

00:08:15.439 --> 00:08:19.069
So who's to say what is and isn't possible with these darn quirks?

00:08:19.289 --> 00:08:25.549
Assuming that he wouldn't die from it, in terms of liters per second, Bakugo is sweating over a million times faster

00:08:25.919 --> 00:08:28.669
Than the average human being. Let that sink in for a minute

00:08:28.669 --> 00:08:35.028
He is sweating a million times faster than you. If you were to stand with that barrel in an Olympic swimming pool,

00:08:35.028 --> 00:08:40.860
He would be able to fill the entire thing with his sweat in 34 minutes and 43 seconds.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:46.520
Every 30 minutes, he's sweating the amount of an Olympic swimming pool. Egh, gross!

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:50.200
Movie Character: "Hey! Sweating is the act of a healthy body."

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:55.000
MP: Of course, Bakugou isn't gonna spend all day in sauna conditions. But even at regular temperatures,

00:08:55.000 --> 00:09:01.740
he'd be sweating buckets on a daily basis; literally sweating buckets! On an average day, a regular person'll produced between

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:09.200
500 and 700 milliliters of sweat. At a million times that rate, Bakugou would be sweating between five and seven hundred

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:12.620
thousand liters every single day.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:18.680
Which, let's be honest, would probably mean he'd need to drink a little bit more than eight glasses of water per day to stay hydrated.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:23.500
And it would definitely mean that I wouldn't want to sit anywhere near him in class or on a bus.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:30.040
Clearly, Bakugo is going in the completely wrong direction when he chose his hero name. Katsuki: "King Explosion Murder."

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:32.260
Midnight: "I'm gonna say that one's a little too violent."

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:38.800
MP: *evil MatPat laugh* Forget all that. With palms sweaty as yours, buddy, you're better off calling yourself the Swamp Thing.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:45.780
But hey! That's just a theory! A film theory! Aaaannndd cut!

